===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=Q23640|:inh|enm:heed<id:head>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|efd}}, {{m|enm|had}}, {{m|enm|hafd}}, {{m|enm|heafd}}, {{m|enm|hed}}, {{m|enm|heed}}, {{m|enm|hefet}}, {{m|enm|heid}}, {{m|enm|het}}, {{m|enm|hevd}}, {{m|enm|heved}}, {{m|enm|hevid}}, {{m|enm|hiede}}, {{m|enm|hæfd}}, {{m|enm|hæfedd}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hēafod|t=head; top; leader; origin}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*haubud}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*haubudą|t=head}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*káput|t=head}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*kap-|t=head; bowl, cup|id=head}}. 

The modern word comes from Old English oblique stem ''hēafd-''; the expected Modern English outcome for ''hēafod'' would be ''*heaved'' (similar to the Middle English word). {{doublet|en|cape|capo|caput|chef|chief|Howth}}.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|heid|t=head}}, {{cog|yol|haade}}, {{m|yol|hade}}, {{m|yol|heade|t=head}}, {{cog|frr|Haur}}, {{m|frr|hood|t=head}}, {{cog|stq|Haud}}, {{m|stq|Hööft|t=head}}, {{cog|fy|haad|t=head}}, {{cog|gsw|Haupt|t=head}}, {{cog|nl|hoofd|t=head}}, {{cog|de|Haupt}}, {{m|de|Häupt|t=head}}, {{cog|wym|hiöet}}, {{m|wym|hiöt}}, {{m|wym|huöt}}, {{m|wym|huø̄t|t=head}}, {{cog|yi|הויפּט|t=head}}, {{cog|da|hode}}, {{m|da|hoved|t=head}}, {{cog|ovd|ovuð|t=head}}, {{cog|fo|høvd}}, {{m|fo|høvur|t=head}}, {{cog|is|höfuð|t=head}}, {{cog|gmq-jmk|huvu|t=head}}, {{cog|nb|hode}}, {{m|nb|hue|t=head}}, {{cog|nn|haud}}, {{m|nn|hauv}}, {{m|nn|hove}}, {{m|nn|hovu}}, {{m|nn|hovud}}, {{m|nn|hue}}, {{m|nn|huggu}}, {{m|nn|hugu}}, {{m|nn|hugud}}, {{m|nn|huvu}}, {{m|nn|huvud|t=head}}, {{cog|gmq-scy|huweð|t=head}}, {{cog|sv|hufvud}}, {{m|sv|hufwud}}, {{m|sv|huve}}, {{m|sv|huvud}}, {{m|sv|hövve|t=head}}, {{cog|gme-cgo|hoef|t=head}}, {{cog|got|𐌷𐌰𐌿𐌱𐌹𐌳}}, {{m|got|𐌷𐌰𐌿𐌱𐌹𐌸|t=head}}; also {{cog|ga,gd|cuach|t=bowl; dome (of head)}}, {{cog|cy|cawg|t=basin, bowl, vessel}}, {{cog|la|capud}}, {{m|la|capus}}, {{m|la|caput|t=head}}, {{cog|el|κεφάλι}}, {{m|el|κεφαλή|t=head}}, {{cog|ckb|کاپۆڵ|t=skull}}, {{cog|sa|कपाल|t=skull; bowl}}.
